            <div xml:id="d358">

                <pb facs="0520" n="396" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg396"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/3578: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-11-18T12:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 18,
                                1921—12 noon</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>299. Your telegram No. 406, November 17. See telegraphic instructions 297,
                    November 17, 5 p.m.<anchor n="88" xml:id="d358-f1"/> You are confidentially
                    informed that reliable information has reached the Department that the Chinese
                    Government has been advised by its Minister here that the payment of its loans
                    without any more delay is extremely urgent.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
